From 1eecb450df809c3775ff740291a2e1ffd6a70575 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:42:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the player information says HDR10+, and what
 was sent of it

The overview page of the player information could not tell HDR10+ from
HDR10: "Format" comes from VideoPlayer.HdrType, the stream's type as the
demuxer gives it, which says HDR10 for HDR10+ (the decoders find HDR10+
picture by picture); "Signal" knew Dolby Vision, PQ, HLG, HDR gamma and
SDR; and "HDR metadata sent" showed only the static metadata. A user had to
photograph the menu of his TV to show that HDR10+ went out.

Now, from the thread that draws (CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::PublishPlayerInfo()):
- "Format" says HDR10+ for an HDR10 stream while the frames handed to the
  window system carry HDR10+ metadata (CWinSystemGbm::HDR10PlusInVideo(),
  set by SetHDR10Plus());
- "Signal" says "HDR10+ (PQ)" while the kernel keeps for HDR10PLUS_VSIF a
  payload that Kodi queued and PQ is signalled: CHDR10PlusOutput::Sent()
  maps the value that the kernel keeps after the last commit it took back to
  the payload queued with it (the newest first: a blob id can come back);
- under "HDR metadata sent", three rows give the values of that payload as
  its InfoFrame codes them (KODI::UTILS::HDR10PLUS::Describe()): the average
  and the 99th percentile of maxRGB (steps of 16 cd/m2), the targeted
  display (not given, or up to 976+), and the tone mapping curve (none, or
  how many anchors).

The strings are new in Estuary's en_gb (32060 to 32063), with es_es, es_ar
and es_mx; the pages of every other skin are made again from Estuary's with
tools/hades-playerinfo/make-playerinfo.py. Native Dolby Vision is not
touched. Host test: hdr10plus_vsif_test.cpp (Sent() and Describe(), 13
checks, which the code before does not have); its pages, pi_check.py (all
seven checks).
